  "verbalization": "Sasanquasaponin I appears to interact with HPAC through a series of molecular targets, with Microtubule-associated protein 1B acting as a common intermediary. This protein is targeted by multiple compounds, including Sasanquasaponin I, Petroraspailyne B1, and (+)-Menthol, all of which ultimately lead to a target interaction with HPAC. The evidence suggests that Sasanquasaponin I may exert its biological effects via a pathway that involves the modulation of Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn influences HPAC through a shared target. The consistent presence of Microtubule-associated protein 1B as a common target across different compounds implies a potential mechanism of action that is not yet fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Microtubule-associated protein 1B in mediating the effects of Sasanquasaponin I on HPAC, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
